{
  "case_id": "2022-22-200",
  "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Slack Technologies)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sections 11 and 12 of the '33 Act expressly reference and enforce the registration statement and prospectus requirements imposed by Section 5 of the Act, 15 U.S.C. 77e. In construing the term \"such security,\" therefore, it's appropriate to look to the meaning of that same term as used in Section 5, the source of the prohibitions enforced by Sections 11 and 12. And it's undisputed that \"such security\" in Section 5 consistently refers only to shares that are subject to registration, never to exempt shares. \"Such security\" in Sections 11 and 12 should be given the same meaning."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: You mentioned 90-year history, but have we had direct listing before?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: All right. So even\nin a situation where you have a prospectus, my\nunderstanding was that a prospectus is a part of\na registration statement, but I suppose it could\nalso be separate. Am I right about that? Like,\nit's a separate document."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can I ask you a\nquestion about Section 11? The former SEC\nofficials' amicus brief suggests that they\nexpected that in a direct listing, the\nregistration statement would cover all the\nsecurities, all the shares, and they say that\nyour position would essentially transform the\n'33 Act into an opt-out regime for direct\nlistings and that we shouldn't do that, and that\nwas contrary to the SEC's expectation when they\ntackled this issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Former SEC officials",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The former SEC\nofficials' amicus brief suggests that they\nexpected that in a direct listing, the\nregistration statement would cover all the\nsecurities, all the shares, and they say that\nyour position would essentially transform the\n'33 Act into an opt-out regime for direct\nlistings and that we shouldn't do that, and that\nwas contrary to the SEC's expectation when they\ntackled this issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the ones who registered them, do you concede that Section 11 liability attached at that point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Kevin K. Russell)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Accordingly, the better view is that \"such security\" in Section 11 refers to all of the shares in the public offering for which the registration statement was a prerequisite."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Kevin K. Russell)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Exceedingly burdensome not only for the parties but also for the courts and the juries who are going to have to determine the registration status of perhaps millions of individual shares of stocks and on the third parties who will be subject to discovery, the -- the brokers, the share depositories, in order to engage in this -- this exercise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You -- you spoke a -- a few moments ago and in the briefs too a bit about this traceability requirement or Section 11 is a standing question, and I -- I just want to clear that up because I -- I -- I for one don't quite see it that way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can't we leave that to the court of appeals to decide whether it was forfeited or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The body of law that they are pointing to simply says you have to show that you purchased under the registered offering that was governed by the registration statement that you said was misleading as opposed to issued under some registration statement a few years earlier that could have been entirely accurate. None of those cases decide the question presented here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Clearly, an exempt security is a security."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there is this question of --of, you know, can Congress or the SEC fix this? Certainly, I think there would be something to fix because, again, the practical consequence of adopting Petitioners' position, I think, is inevitably going to open the door to this -- their strategem of letting in a few exempt shares, even in traditional IPOs, and arguing that, therefore, you have to trace. And that's generally going to be impossible."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2022-22-200",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "14d8144526f806862fff2ad0398509fd907dcc5987f98dd861dec8e58dff2157",
      "evidence_id": "ev-14d8144526f8-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The SEC's position is perfectly clear."
    },
